  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_0' aria-label=\" Chhaganbhai Kohyabhai Pateliya and Others versus The State of Gujarat and Others pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('0','2026','2026_10_295_302',''); ><font size='4'> <strong>CHHAGANBHAI KOHYABHAI PATELIYA AND OTHERS<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>THE STATE OF GUJARAT AND OTHERS </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 10 S.C.R. 295</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010003412026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : SANJEEV SACHDEVA<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, SANJAY KUMAR</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Issue arose whether the appellants-daily-wage skilled workers could be denied the benefit of increment when they were treated as permanent employees for the purpose of payscale and allowances, pension, retirement benefits. Headnotes&dagger; Service law and pensionary benefits &ndash; Claim of &ndash; Appellants, daily-wage skilled workers rendered over 30 years of service and retired on 30th June in different years &ndash; Workers claimed the benefit of annual increment which fell due on 1st July of those years, after their retirement<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 06-10-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 13454/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Appeal(s) allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('0','2026','2026_10_295_302','','S')><img src='images/split_24.svg' alt='' aria-hidden='true'>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a hr